---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { COPY } from '../../lib/ui.ts';
import type { Locale } from '../../lib/locales.ts';

interface Props { locale: Locale }
const { locale } = Astro.props;
const c = COPY[locale];
---
<Base locale={locale} title={c.navAbout} description={c.tagline} path="/about" current="about">
  <h1>About Antar</h1>
  <p class="lede">{c.tagline}</p>

  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>
    Antar records what the government said it would achieve, measures what has happened using the
    government's own published data, and shows the distance between the two. Every figure carries the
    document it came from, the date it was retrieved, and the name of the person who checked it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>अंतर</strong> means the distance between two things.
  </p>

  <h2>What it is not</h2>
  <p>
    It is not a scorecard, a ranking, or an assessment of whether any government is doing well. It
    does not say whether a target is worth pursuing, who is to blame for a shortfall, or what you
    should conclude. Where context is needed, it is attributed to whoever said it — never asserted here.
  </p>
  <p>
    News coverage of government performance is rarely wrong about the facts. It goes wrong by mixing
    sourced facts with unsourced interpretation until the two cannot be separated. This site tries not
    to have that seam at all.
  </p>

  <h2>Who runs it</h2>
  <p>
    Nishtha Sharma. One person, who is currently the author, the verifier and the only reviewer. That
    is a real weakness and it is written down rather than hidden: the
    <a href="https://github.com/nishtha2403/antar/blob/main/SUCCESSION.md">succession clause</a>
    records that nobody can currently remove the founder, and that publication stops entirely if she
    is unavailable.
  </p>

  <h2>How to check it, or argue with it</h2>
  <p>
    Every record is public and every figure links to its source. A disagreement can be settled by
    reading the same document rather than by trusting this site. If something here is wrong, it will
    appear on the <a href="corrections">corrections page</a> — corrections are appended and never
    deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>What it will never accept</h2>
  <p>
    Political party funding. Any funder's influence over a metric. Requests to suppress inconvenient
    data. These are written into the project's
    <a href="https://github.com/nishtha2403/antar/blob/main/CONSTITUTION.md">constitution</a>, which
    also records honestly which of its rules the code enforces and which rest on trust.
  </p>
</Base>
